# Unit 1: Introduction to Python, Strings and Numbers

## Overview

Welcome to Unit 1!

This unit introduces the foundations of Python programming and shows how Python can be used to solve real-world problems in different industries.

In this unit, I will learn how to set up a Python development environment, write and run basic Python programs, and understand how Python stores and represents different types of information.

I will also learn about variables and basic data types such as strings, integers, floats, and booleans. These concepts form an important foundation for the programming skills I will develop throughout the rest of the course.

## Learning Objectives

By the end of this unit, I should be able to:

- Explain what Python is and identify three real-world applications of Python.
- Set up a working Python development environment.
- Write and run a basic Python program using `print()` and `input()`.
- Declare variables using the appropriate data types: `str`, `int`, `float`, and `bool`.
- Use `type()` to identify the data type of a value.

## What I Will Practise

During this unit, I will practise:

- Writing my first Python programs.
- Using `print()` to display information.
- Using `input()` to receive information from a user.
- Creating and assigning variables.
- Working with strings and numbers.
- Identifying different Python data types.
- Using `type()` to check data types.

## Next Steps

After completing this unit, I will move on to the video lesson, review the lesson notes, and complete the practical task and quiz to test my understanding.
